{
  "dom_id": "step-q59968",
  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130839/assets/e29b109de404ddd4b379a78d0c890f4bf2894bb7bac052757be41058382c4ffb.png)\n\nWhat picture is missing from the multiplication model above?",
  "worked_solution": "In the model, we have $\\frac{2}{3}$ on the left.\n\nSince we need to multiply by $\\frac{2}{3}$, we split the whole into $3$ equal parts horizontally and ensure that $2$ of the parts remain shaded.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130839/assets/94f565afb7763feb8aa433f6f355fdd3249059a7b2c943be569c01cd2b15b426.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{4}{9}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore, the missing picture is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130839/assets/a4f11a6866d6b855123d340319bc8dc4a3d39b8f5a1dd42846a549c123eab295.png)",
